# NOTE (4.9.2026): Cloudflare Pages ignores 404 rules in this file — verified live:
# /scripts/* answered 200 with a 404 rule in place. Every 404 line below is
# therefore a *map*, and the real block is a Function stub under functions/
# re-exporting functions/_deny.js. tests/site.test.mjs fails if a 404 path
# here has no stub.
# Only non-obvious redirects live here.
# CF Pages serves .html files and index.html in subdirs automatically.

# Internal working docs + analytics data live in the repo root (the deploy
# root) — serve 404 instead of exposing them. robots.txt entries would only
# advertise the paths; this actually blocks them.
# Three of these were listed and four were not, which is the failure mode of a
# list that is maintained by hand: the ones added later were simply forgotten.
# Everything in the repo is deployed (there is no .cfignore), so any file added
# to the root is public the moment it is committed.
/ANALYTICS.md         /404.html   404
/BACKLOG.md           /404.html   404
/PRODUCT_OVERVIEW.md  /404.html   404
/COORDINATION.md      /404.html   404
/ROADMAP.md           /404.html   404
/ELECTRICAL_KIT.md    /404.html   404
/README.md            /404.html   404
/data/clarity/*       /404.html   404
# Build-only inputs: the IEC tables feed scripts/build_iec_block.py and the
# field-research notes feed the eval scripts. Nothing at runtime fetches them.
# data/materials/* and data/coverage/* stay public — the Functions read those.
/data/iec_calculator.csv  /404.html   404
/data/iec_full.json       /404.html   404
/data/iec_map_block.txt   /404.html   404
/data/field-research/*    /404.html   404
# Shared header/footer fragments: stamped into the pages at build time by
# scripts/stamp_partials.mjs, never served on their own.
/partials/*           /404.html   404
# The security review's own notes: how the CSP was verified and what it does and
# does not cover. Publishing the review of the defences alongside the defences
# is the one file on this list that actually helps an attacker.
/scripts/*            /404.html   404

/app    /sale/    301
# The helper screen has a door of its own — the link Stav sends a friend.
/help   /sale/?panel=helper   302
/Help   /sale/?panel=helper   302
/HELP   /sale/?panel=helper   302
/עזרה   /sale/?panel=helper   302

# The standalone periodic-checkups page was retired (4.9.2026): the screen
# lives inside the app. The URL was already sent to customers on WhatsApp and
# sits in bookmarks, so it keeps landing somewhere.
/checkups    /sale/    301
/checkups/*  /sale/    301

# Case tolerance for the shared /ask/ link (people type it by hand from WhatsApp)
/ASK    /ask/    301
/ASK/*  /ask/    301
/Ask    /ask/    301
/Ask/*  /ask/    301
# V3 working docs — not part of the public site
/docs/* /404.html 404
